│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_ring_ansatz                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 24 distinct trainable angles, including 16 independently          │
│                          │ parameterized RZ gates surrounding an open CZ chain. Because RZ and CZ are diagonal in    │
│                          │ the same basis, much of that structure is redundant, while the large parameter count      │
│                          │ encourages overfitting and reduces parameter efficiency.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new ansatz uses only three distinct parameters: separate RY angles for even and odd   │
│                          │ wires and one globally shared RX mixing angle. A closed, alternating CZ ring gives every  │
│                          │ qubit equal connectivity and avoids edge-specific behavior that can weaken the            │
│                          │ worst-group margin. The RX layer does not commute with the CZ entanglers, so it provides  │
│                          │ useful basis mixing without per-wire parameters. Compared with the original block, this   │
│                          │ configuration reduces the distinct parameter count from 24 to 3, lowers gate count and    │
│                          │ expected depth, and imposes a strong translational/parity-based inductive bias intended   │
│                          │ to improve few-sample generalization, convergence, and robust separation. Learning rates  │
│                          │ and iteration counts remain controlled by the fixed external training loop.               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
