│ patch_description        │ This design preserves distinct RY parameters so every qubit can learn its own             │
│                          │ feature-mixing angle, while imposing reflection symmetry only on the phase layers. Qubits │
│                          │ in mirror pairs (0,7), (1,6), (2,5), and (3,4) share their pre-entanglement and           │
│                          │ post-entanglement RZ parameters. This reduces the ansatz from 24 to 16 distinct           │
│                          │ parameters without enforcing the overly restrictive global or parity sharing seen in the  │
│                          │ current program. The fixed nearest-neighbor CZ chain retains the strong generalization,   │
│                          │ margin, and convergence behavior of the original architecture while the structured        │
│                          │ sharing improves parameter efficiency and regularizes training on the small dataset.      │
