│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses three distinct parameters, duplicates the entire butterfly block, │
│                          │ and reaches a depth of 30 without improving the worst-group margin enough to offset its   │
│                          │ higher parameter and gate costs. This proposal returns to one multiscale pass with        │
│                          │ globally shared local RY and RX parameters, reducing depth and avoiding parity-specific   │
│                          │ overfitting. Two distance-4 CZ gates are replaced by XX interactions sharing one          │
│                          │ `global_xx` angle. This adds a single economical long-range correlation parameter while   │
│                          │ preserving the remaining CZ butterfly structure. The noncommuting XX couplings should     │
│                          │ improve separation of difficult samples, while the compact block should generalize and    │
