│ patch_description        │ This design retains the parameter-efficient global mixing and multiscale butterfly        │
│                          │ connectivity that performed best, while replacing the fixed distance-2 CZ layer with      │
│                          │ tunable CRZ interactions. Rather than adding a third parameter, the medium-range phase    │
│                          │ couplings share `phase_readout` with the final RX layer. This phase-locks correlation     │
│                          │ generation to its noncommuting readout conversion, yielding richer dynamics while         │
│                          │ preserving only two distinct trainable parameters. The resulting strongly regularized,    │
│                          │ low-dimensional optimization should converge reliably and may improve worst-group         │
│                          │ separation without sacrificing parameter efficiency.                                      │
