│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_staggered_butterfly                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This design retains the parameter-efficient global RY/RX controls and multiscale          │
│                          │ butterfly connectivity that performed well previously, but changes when information is    │
│                          │ mixed. Even-indexed qubits receive the shared RY rotation first, followed by              │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor CZ gates that couple them to still-unmixed odd qubits. The odd-indexed   │
│                          │ rotations are then applied, creating a staggered symmetry breaking without adding         │
│                          │ parameters. Distance-2 and distance-4 CZ layers subsequently propagate these              │
│                          │ heterogeneous local responses globally, while the final shared RX layer exposes phase     │
│                          │ correlations to later repetitions and readout. The ansatz preserves two distinct          │
│                          │ trainable parameters while aiming for better worst-group separation and gradient flow.    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
