│ patch_description        │ Remove the redundant in-spec repetition, since the fixed architecture already repeats the │
│                          │ ansatz externally with tied parameters. This halves ansatz depth and gate count, reducing │
│                          │ overprocessing and convergence cost. Reallocate the existing three-parameter budget from  │
│                          │ parity-specific input rotations to one strongly regularized global RY mixer plus separate │
│                          │ left/right RX tilts. The half-specific output basis allows asymmetric phase-to-population │
│                          │ conversion across the two four-qubit partitions, potentially improving the hardest-group  │
│                          │ margin without increasing the current distinct parameter count.                           │
