│ patch_description        │ Tie the final RX layer back to the same global parameter used by the RY mixers. The       │
│                          │ current staggered butterfly layout already improves validation margin and worst-group     │
│                          │ margin, while the second distinct parameter lowers parameter efficiency enough to reduce  │
│                          │ the combined score. Sharing one angle preserves the noncommuting phase-to-population      │
│                          │ conversion and current gate topology while restoring the stronger one-parameter           │
│                          │ regularization prior, reducing overfitting risk and simplifying optimization.             │
