│ patch_description        │ This design keeps the strongest observed regularizer—one globally shared parameter—but    │
│                          │ replaces fixed CZ entanglement with hierarchical parity-echo gadgets. Each CNOT–RY–CNOT   │
│                          │ sequence conjugates a local rotation into a trainable two-qubit parity interaction        │
│                          │ without adding another parameter. Three butterfly scales capture local, four-qubit, and   │
│                          │ cross-half correlations, while their echoed structure limits uncontrolled feature         │
│                          │ scrambling. A final shared RX layer converts the learned parity information into the      │
│                          │ measurement basis. The resulting circuit is an asymmetric, multiscale one-parameter       │
│                          │ quantum walk intended to improve hard-group separation while preserving parameter         │
│                          │ efficiency and small-sample generalization.                                               │
